{
    "version": "Antigravity CLI 1.5.15, `agy acp`",
    "source": "Recorded with tee-cli.ts in front of `agy acp` 1.5.15 (AGY_CLI_DISABLE_AUTO_UPDATE=1), driven by ADE CORE's ACP backend in supervised mode in a throwaway git folder, with a local stand-in for Ruimte's MCP route. `initialize` answers protocol 1, `agentInfo` \"Antigravity ACP Server\" 1.5.15, `loadSession` and `sessionCapabilities` resume, close, load, list and additionalDirectories (each also under snake_case keys), `auth.logout`, four auth methods, and no `mcpCapabilities`, although an http server passed in `session/new` is used. `session/new` answers modes default, accept-edits, auto and plan (no yolo, no auto_edit) and config options model, thought_level (low to xhigh) and mode; only two models are kept here. A Ruimte tool comes as a `tool_call` with `name` `mcp_ruimte_node_list`, title `Run mcp_ruimte_node_list`, kind `other`, `rawInput` holding only agy's `toolSummary`; agy asks `session/request_permission` (allow, deny) for it in default mode, then sends in_progress and completed with no output content. There is no `call_mcp_tool` in this session: asked for the other call shape, the model says so and calls `mcp_ruimte_echo_text` again. A command is `name` `run_command`, kind `execute`, title the command line, with `rawOutput.output` and `exit_code`. Usage: `usage_update` (used, size 1048576) after each step, and the prompt response carries `usage` with inputTokens, outputTokens, cachedReadTokens, cachedWriteTokens, thoughtTokens and totalTokens, where totalTokens is input + cachedRead + output (output already holds the thoughts). `mcp` is what the MCP route received: first `server/discover` with header MCP-Protocol-Version 2026-07-28 and no `initialize` before it; on a JSON-RPC error agy sends `initialize` with protocolVersion 2025-11-25, `notifications/initialized`, two GETs, `tools/list`, and `notifications/roots/list_changed` twice at each session start and turn end, never an MCP session id. `mcpAfter400` is a second agy (session/new only) whose server answers `server/discover` with HTTP 400 as Ruimte's route does: agy falls back to `initialize` 2025-11-25 within 1 ms. `hooks` are the Stop hooks agy's global hook config posted during the run, one per turn. `agy --help` (1.5.15) still has `--conversation <id>`, `-i`/`--prompt-interactive`, `--mode` (accept-edits, auto, plan) and `--dangerously-skip-permissions`; `agy acp --help` adds `--login` (\"Log in with Google interactively, then exit (ACP terminal auth)\"), `--add-dir` and `--process-per-session`. Thought chunks are left out, consecutive message chunks are merged into one. `t` is milliseconds from the start, `dir` is `in` for what went to agy.",
